  <h1>Oryx: Switching Between Attention and Linear Recurrence Mid-Sequence</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    What if a language model could use quadratic attention for the retrieval-heavy parts of a sequence, and flip to a linear recurrent model for the rest — at inference time, without retraining? Oryx makes this possible by tying 90%+ of parameters across softmax attention and linear RNN (Mamba-2 / Gated DeltaNet) variants, so both mechanisms share internal representations and can hand off to each other seamlessly.
  </p>
